<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Order of Aviz</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">12th century–</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Order of Avis</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Order of Aviz was a Portuguese military religious order founded in the twelfth century to fight the Moors, taking its name from its seat at Aviz in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alentejo">Alentejo</a>, granted in 1211. Following the Cistercian rule, it took part in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reconquista">Reconquista</a> of southern Portugal. John, Master of Aviz, became king as John I in 1385, giving his name to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-aviz">House of Aviz</a>. It survives as an honorary order of merit.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/order-of-aviz.jpg" alt="Order of Aviz" width="320" height="406" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: RS1974 · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ordem_Honor%C3%ADfica_Portuguesa_-_Ordem_Militar_de_Avis.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
